  usage: ddflow help [-h] [topic]
  
  positional arguments:
    topic       one of: cli, config, customise, export, gates, import, mcp, memory, parallel,
                recovery, verify, workflow. Omit for the overview.
  
  options:
    -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow history]
  '''
  usage: ddflow history [-h] [--item ITEM] [--kind KIND] [--since SINCE] [--limit LIMIT] [--agent LOG_AGENT] [--tail TAIL]
  
  options:
    -h, --help         show this help message and exit
    --item ITEM        restrict to one item
    --kind KIND        comma-separated event kinds or families: 'gate', 'lease.acquired',
                       'decision,bug'
    --since SINCE      ISO timestamp lower bound
    --limit LIMIT
    --agent LOG_AGENT  only this agent's shard
    --tail TAIL        the last N events, oldest first
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow hooks check-commit]
  '''
  usage: ddflow hooks check-commit [-h]
  
  options:
    -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow hooks check-msg]
  '''
  usage: ddflow hooks check-msg [-h] msg_file
  
  positional arguments:
    msg_file    the message file git passes the hook
  
  options:
    -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow hooks install]
  '''
  usage: ddflow hooks install [-h] [--force] [--claude] [--gemini]
  
  options:
    -h, --help  show this help message and exit
    --force     replace an existing pre-commit hook ddflow does not manage
    --claude    the Claude Code SessionStart hook in .claude/settings.json instead of the git hook;
                other hooks there are left exactly as they are
    --gemini    the Gemini CLI BeforeAgent prompt hook in .gemini/settings.json
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow hooks pre-compact]
  '''
  usage: ddflow hooks pre-compact [-h]
  
  options:
    -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow hooks prompt]
  '''
  usage: ddflow hooks prompt [-h] [--gemini]
  
  options:
    -h, --help  show this help message and exit
    --gemini    answer with the JSON Gemini CLI wants
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow hooks session-start]
  '''
  usage: ddflow hooks session-start [-h]
  
  options:
    -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow hooks status]
  '''
  usage: ddflow hooks status [-h]
  
  options:
    -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow hooks uninstall]
  '''
  usage: ddflow hooks uninstall [-h] [--claude] [--gemini]
  
  options:
    -h, --help  show this help message and exit
    --claude    the Claude Code SessionStart hook in .claude/settings.json instead of the git hook;
                other hooks there are left exactly as they are
    --gemini    the Gemini CLI BeforeAgent prompt hook in .gemini/settings.json
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow hooks]
  '''
  usage: ddflow hooks [-h] {install,uninstall,status,check-commit,check-msg,session-start,pre-compact,prompt} ...
  
  positional arguments:
    {install,uninstall,status,check-commit,check-msg,session-start,pre-compact,prompt}
      check-commit        (invoked by the hook)
      check-msg           (invoked by the commit-msg hook)
      session-start       (invoked by the Claude Code SessionStart hook) print the brief; always
                          exit 0
      pre-compact         (invoked by the Claude Code PreCompact hook) record what the session was
                          doing before compaction; always exit 0
      prompt              (invoked by the UserPromptSubmit / BeforeAgent hook) record the prompt on
                          stdin; always exit 0
  
  options:
    -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow import]
  '''
  usage: ddflow import [-h] [--apply] [--verify] [--include-done] [--max-tasks MAX_TASKS]
  
  options:
    -h, --help            show this help message and exit
    --apply               write them; default is a dry run
    --verify              report what was already imported and whether it is still true: source
                          drift, vanished source files, and the globs and decisions the import left
                          for a human (exit 1 = findings, 2 = nothing imported)
    --include-done        also import already-ticked items, as completed. Off by default: a finished
                          history is not a queue.
    --max-tasks MAX_TASKS
                          refuse to propose more tasks than this. 0 (the default) uses [importer]
                          max_tasks from the config, which ships at 200. A bigger number is usually
                          a whole history rather than a queue.
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow init]
  '''
  usage: ddflow init [-h]
  
  options:
    -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow job add]
  '''
  usage: ddflow job add [-h] --pid PID [--command COMMAND] [--log LOG] item
  
  positional arguments:
    item
  
  options:
    -h, --help         show this help message and exit
    --pid PID
    --command COMMAND
    --log LOG
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow job end]
  '''
  usage: ddflow job end [-h] [--exit-code EXIT_CODE] [--note NOTE] [--force] job
  
  positional arguments:
    job
  
  options:
    -h, --help            show this help message and exit
    --exit-code EXIT_CODE
                          default: the one its log recorded
    --note NOTE
    --force               end a job on another host you have checked there
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow job list]
  '''
  usage: ddflow job list [-h] [--item ITEM] [--all]
  
  options:
    -h, --help   show this help message and exit
    --item ITEM
    --all        include ended jobs
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow job run]
  '''
  usage: ddflow job run [-h] [--log LOG] [--cwd CWD] item command
  
  positional arguments:
    item
    command     shell command (quote it)
  
  options:
    -h, --help  show this help message and exit
    --log LOG   output file (default .ddflow/local/jobs/)
    --cwd CWD   default: the item's worktree, else the repo
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow job]
  '''
  usage: ddflow job [-h] {run,add,list,end} ...
  
  positional arguments:
    {run,add,list,end}
      run               launch a command detached for an item and record it
      add               register a process started some other way
      list              jobs with their live status (exit 2 = none)
      end               record how a job ended (refused while it runs)
  
  options:
    -h, --help          show this help message and exit
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow lesson add]
  '''
  usage: ddflow lesson add [-h] [--id ID] --title TITLE [--rule RULE] [--why WHY] [--how HOW] [--summary SUMMARY] [--tags TAGS] [--seen-in SEEN_IN] [--supersedes SUPERSEDES] [--pattern PATTERN] [--globs GLOBS] [--new | --extends ID | --duplicate-of ID | --related ID | --check]
  
  options:
    -h, --help            show this help message and exit
    --id ID
    --title TITLE
    --rule RULE
    --why WHY
    --how HOW
    --summary SUMMARY     the lesson in one paragraph; what docs/ddflow/LESSONS-SUMMARY.md is made
                          of
    --tags TAGS
    --seen-in SEEN_IN
    --supersedes SUPERSEDES
    --pattern PATTERN     regex this lesson forbids. Scans NOW and stores WHICH sites match, so
                          `lesson verify` can name what reappeared — a count could only say it got
                          worse
    --globs GLOBS         comma-separated globs to scan (default: all tracked files)
    --new                 answer a possible-duplicate refusal: this is a different record, file it
    --extends ID          answer it: this adds to record ID -- appended to ID while it is open and
                          unclaimed, else filed as a new record linked to it
    --duplicate-of ID     answer it: this is the same thing as record ID (handled like --extends)
    --related ID          answer it: a different record that is related to ID; linked both ways
    --check               dry run: print the existing records this would be refused as a duplicate
                          of and write nothing (exit 0 with candidates, 2 with none)
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow lesson list]
  '''
  usage: ddflow lesson list [-h] [--state STATE] [--tag TAG] [--owner OWNER] [--since SINCE] [--limit LIMIT] [--all]
  
  options:
    -h, --help     show this help message and exit
    --state STATE  only rows in this state
    --tag TAG      only rows carrying this tag
    --owner OWNER  only rows leased by this agent (not --agent, which is who YOU are)
    --since SINCE  only rows last changed at or after this ISO date or timestamp
    --limit LIMIT  most rows to show (default 50)
    --all          include superseded lessons
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow lesson search]
  '''
  usage: ddflow lesson search [-h] [--limit LIMIT] query
  
  positional arguments:
    query
  
  options:
