# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow research]
  '''
  usage: ddflow research [-h] [--id ID] [--question QUESTION] [--claim CLAIM] [--mechanism MECHANISM] [--falsifier FALSIFIER] [--probe PROBE] [--probe-output PROBE_OUTPUT] [--verdict VERDICT] [--sources SOURCES] [--budget BUDGET] [--item ITEM] [--new | --extends ID | --duplicate-of ID | --related ID | --check] [--state STATE] [--phase PHASE] [--tag TAG] [--since SINCE] [--limit LIMIT] [{add,list}]
  
  positional arguments:
    {add,list}            optional: `research add` = `research`; `research list` lists the notes
  
  options:
    -h, --help            show this help message and exit
    --id ID
    --question QUESTION
    --claim CLAIM
    --mechanism MECHANISM
    --falsifier FALSIFIER
    --probe PROBE
    --probe-output PROBE_OUTPUT
    --verdict VERDICT
    --sources SOURCES
    --budget BUDGET
    --item ITEM
    --new                 answer a possible-duplicate refusal: this is a different record, file it
    --extends ID          answer it: this adds to record ID -- appended to ID while it is open and
                          unclaimed, else filed as a new record linked to it
    --duplicate-of ID     answer it: this is the same thing as record ID (handled like --extends)
    --related ID          answer it: a different record that is related to ID; linked both ways
    --check               dry run: print the existing records this would be refused as a duplicate
                          of and write nothing (exit 0 with candidates, 2 with none)
    --state STATE         only rows in this state
    --phase PHASE         only rows under this phase id
    --tag TAG             only rows carrying this tag
    --since SINCE         only rows last changed at or after this ISO date or timestamp
    --limit LIMIT         most rows to show (default 50)
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow resolve]
  '''
  usage: ddflow resolve [-h] --keep KEEP [--refile-as REFILE_AS] id
  
  positional arguments:
    id
  
  options:
    -h, --help            show this help message and exit
    --keep KEEP           the definition's event id (or a 6+ character prefix), or the agent / lease
                          holder, to keep — `ddflow show <id>` lists them
    --refile-as REFILE_AS
                          re-add each definition NOT kept under these new ids (comma-separated, in
                          `show` order) in the same transaction
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow review]
  '''
  usage: ddflow review [-h] [--gate GATE] [--intent INTENT] [--context CONTEXT] [--base BASE] [--commit COMMIT] [--branch BRANCH] [--chunk CHUNK] [--delta] [--full] [--force] [--reason REASON] [--finding FINDING] [--refuted] [--confirmed] [--probe PROBE] [id ...]
  
  positional arguments:
    id                 the item; or `triage <item>`
  
  options:
    -h, --help         show this help message and exit
    --gate GATE        gate to review (default critic); rubber_duck,critic reviews both -- one
                       combined review under [review].combined_under_lines changed lines
    --intent INTENT    what the change is meant to do (defaults to the item's title/body)
    --context CONTEXT
    --base BASE
    --commit COMMIT    review this one landed commit (vs its first parent) instead of the item's
                       branch
    --branch BRANCH    review this branch against base -- for an item claimed without a worktree
                       (default: the branch checked out in the worktree you are standing in)
    --chunk CHUNK      re-review only chunk N (as the recorded review numbered it; repeatable, or
                       '2,5') and merge it into that record -- same diff, chunk size and reviewer
    --delta            recheck ONLY what changed since the head the gate's last review covered, for
                       a diff too large to send twice: not a full round, but counted against
                       [review].max_rounds. A plain re-review is a full round with the previous
                       findings; [review].delta_default = true makes it a delta instead
    --full             review the item's WHOLE diff even when [review].delta_default would make it a
                       delta: a full round, counted against [review].max_rounds
    --force            run a full round past [review].max_rounds; needs --reason, recorded in the
                       evidence
    --reason REASON    why --force
    --finding FINDING  triage: the finding's number (#N)
    --refuted          triage: --probe shows the finding is false
    --confirmed        triage: --probe is the fix/test that answers it
    --probe PROBE      triage: the evidence for the verdict
  
  two commands share this parser:
    ddflow review <id> --gate G [--chunk N | --delta]   run the reviewer(s) (slow, shared);
                    a gate gets [review].max_rounds (default 2) rounds, full or delta, then triage
    ddflow review triage <id> --gate G --finding N --refuted|--confirmed --probe ...
                                              record what became of one finding
  --finding/--refuted/--confirmed/--probe belong to the second form only. It REQUIRES the
  `triage` verb: without it they are refused, never run as a review.
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow reviewers add]
  '''
  usage: ddflow reviewers add [-h] [--preset PRESET] [--name NAME] [--model MODEL] [--base-url BASE_URL] [--gates GATES] [--shared] [--no-launch]
  
  options:
    -h, --help           show this help message and exit
    --preset PRESET      see `ddflow reviewers presets`
    --name NAME
    --model MODEL
    --base-url BASE_URL
    --gates GATES
    --shared             write to the committed .ddflow/config.toml instead of the git-ignored
                         .ddflow/local/reviewers.toml -- only for a reviewer every clone should use
    --no-launch          do not auto-start a local server for this reviewer
  
  '''
