# ---
# name: test_help[ddflow]
  '''
  usage: ddflow [-h] [--repo REPO] [--agent AGENT] [--json] [--allow-older-version] [--reason SKEW_REASON] [--version] {init,phase,task,split,resolve,update,next,claim,heartbeat,release,wait,approve,gate,complete,abandon,remove,block,unblock,merge,pr,version,promote,flow,brief,external,job,memory,lesson,recall,similar,dupes,link,decision,rule,verify,ci,onboard,status,research,bug,session,replay,recover,progress,loops,cleanup,doctor,rebuild,render,board,show,config,upgrade,export,bisect,cadence,pins,tests,precommit,reviewers,review,adopt,history,workflow,help,import,companions,prompts,hooks,mcp,search} ...
  
  A portable work-queue kernel for AI coding agents. The event log is the source of truth;
  everything else is derived.
  
  positional arguments:
    {init,phase,task,split,resolve,update,next,claim,heartbeat,release,wait,approve,gate,complete,abandon,remove,block,unblock,merge,pr,version,promote,flow,brief,external,job,memory,lesson,recall,similar,dupes,link,decision,rule,verify,ci,onboard,status,research,bug,session,replay,recover,progress,loops,cleanup,doctor,rebuild,render,board,show,config,upgrade,export,bisect,cadence,pins,tests,precommit,reviewers,review,adopt,history,workflow,help,import,companions,prompts,hooks,mcp,search}
      init                create .ddflow/ in this repository
      phase               add a phase
      task                add a task
      split               split an item into sub-tasks in place, keeping its id and history
      resolve             settle a CONTESTED item (rival adds or claims from two clones), on the
                          record
      update              change an item's fields
      next                what may start now (exit 2 = nothing actionable, exit 1 = unknown --phase)
      claim               lease an item + create its worktree (exit 3 = refused)
      heartbeat           renew a lease
      release             give up a lease
      wait                sleep until an item (or anything) can be claimed; exit 2 = deadline, or
                          waiting cannot help
      approve             a PERSON clears (or rejects) a human-approval gate — no MCP equivalent
      gate                run / record / inspect a gate
      complete            finish an item (exit 3 = gates not satisfied)
      abandon             stop work on an item without completing it
      remove              take an item out of the queue (recorded, not erased)
      unblock             release a blocked item back into the queue (exit 2 = not blocked)
      merge               merge an item's branch from the primary checkout
      pr                  pull/merge requests: what reviewers did ([flow].integration = pr)
      version             version tags: the next version, and cutting it
      promote             environment branches: move work one step downstream ([flow].environments)
      flow                how this project works: branching model, release lines, and every workflow
                          choice with who made it
      brief               budgeted session-start pack
      external            dependencies on items in sibling repositories
      job                 long-running processes an item waits on: run, add, list, end
      memory              operational facts about this machine/repo, shown at session start
      recall              'have we been here before?' — search decisions, lessons, research, bugs,
                          tasks and past prompts at once
      similar             'is this already filed?' -- the existing bugs, tasks, lessons and other
                          records most like a text, before you add it (read-only; exit 2 when none)
      dupes               'is anything filed twice?' -- the near-duplicate PAIRS already in the log,
                          skipping pairs already linked or dismissed (read-only; exit 2 when none)
      link                settle a near-duplicate pair: say how one record relates to another
      decision            architectural decisions: record and consult
      rule                project rules: add, edit, list, search, show, remove
      verify              re-derive the claims behind a done task, or sweep them all (exit 1 = one
                          fails)
      ci                  the CI parity gate: run the pre-push checks on the merge result
      onboard             run an onboarding stage: one report, propose by default
                          (status|preflight|legacy|memory|test-gate|verify)
      status              one answer to 'what is the state of this project?'
      replay              reconstruct the decision history from the log
      recover             find crashed agents' work (exit 2 = nothing)
      progress            work actually done, aggregated from the log
      loops               circular references and runtime loops (exit 2 = none)
      cleanup             classify ddflow worktrees/branches; --apply lands the safe ones
      doctor              integrity + health check
      rebuild             re-derive the index from the log
      render              regenerate the human-readable views
      config              print every knob, its value and its source
      upgrade             what upgrading this project to the running ddflow would change (the plan;
                          writes nothing; exit 0 up to date, 1 pending)
      export              documents generated from the log: list, print, enable, disable, --diff,
                          --check, --update
      bisect              find which earlier test file makes a test fail only in full-suite order
                          (exit 0 = found, 2 = nothing to report)
      cadence             which periodic passes are due (exit 2 = none)
      pins                which text of an instruction file a test pins, before you compress it
      tests               the tests your change reaches, and a parallel command to run them (exit 2
                          = none)
      precommit           propose a .pre-commit-config.yaml for this repository's stacks (writes
                          nothing without --write)
      reviewers           find, list and test cross-family reviewers
      review              run the configured reviewer(s) over an item's diff
      adopt               install ddflow into this project for one or more agents
      history             one timeline of everything that happened (exit 2 = nothing)
      workflow            the rules this project runs by, and how to change them (exit 1 =
                          incoherent)
      help                what ddflow is, what it can do, and the workflow (try: ddflow help
                          workflow)
      import              propose the existing project's work, lessons and decisions (exit 2 =
                          nothing)
      companions          companion MCP servers that serve the gates (exit 2 = a default one is
                          missing)
      prompts             inspect and override the prompt templates
      hooks               install/inspect the enforcement git hook and the Claude Code session hook
      mcp                 run the MCP stdio server over this repository
      search              search tasks, phases, bugs, research, decisions, lessons, sessions,
                          prompts and the log (exit 2 = no match)
  
  options:
    -h, --help            show this help message and exit
    --repo REPO           repository root (default: cwd, resolved to the primary checkout)
    --agent AGENT         agent identity (default: host-pid). Shards the log.
    --json                machine-readable output
    --allow-older-version
                          let THIS session write although this ddflow is older than the one that
                          last worked on the log (the skew guard); needs --reason, is recorded, and
                          only the operator's insistence justifies it
    --reason SKEW_REASON  with --allow-older-version: why (a command's own --reason is used if it
                          has one)
    --version             print the version and exit
  
  '''
# ---
